 "reading": "A check that takes the unchanged callee as one function gets its candidate from the conversion alone: any password with a unit from 0x80 up, with any salt. Four of the seven salts of the claim's assumption are invalid and throw IllegalArgumentException on both sides whatever the password, a null password throws on both sides, and a difference past the 72nd byte never reaches the result. A candidate from the abstraction is a witness only once the real cipher has shown two results, so the search must be able to drop a candidate that does not replay and try another, or prefer a valid salt and a difference within the first 72 bytes."
